===Etymology===
American English, of {{unk|en|title=unknown}} origin; perhaps from {{der|en|el|μαλακία||stupidity, idiocy, nonsense, bullshit}}. Popularized by Thomas Aloysius Dorgan, Irish American cartoonist who started using it in cartoons on March 9, 1922.<ref>[https://www.npr.org/sections/thetwo-way/2012/10/12/162791655/whats-all-this-malarkey-about-malarkey| NPR’s All this Malarkey]</ref>

